WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.095 --> 00:00:03.174
(camera focusing)

00:00:03.174 --> 00:00:05.061
(bug skittering)

00:00:05.061 --> 00:00:08.871
- [Voiceover] This here
is a darkling beetle.

00:00:08.871 --> 00:00:13.215
It lives out here in the vast
desert of northwest Utah.

00:00:13.215 --> 00:00:15.598
And he is on the move.

00:00:15.598 --> 00:00:16.431
Where to?

00:00:17.306 --> 00:00:19.207
I don't have a clue.

00:00:19.207 --> 00:00:22.245
But I can tell you about the
town he's leaving behind.

00:00:22.245 --> 00:00:23.948
(quiet country-western music)

00:00:23.948 --> 00:00:25.865
Welcome to Lucin, Utah.

00:00:27.168 --> 00:00:29.668
There's abandoned cars, weeds.

00:00:31.065 --> 00:00:33.640
Once in a while, a
train will pass through.

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:34.637
(distant train whistle)

00:00:34.637 --> 00:00:38.089
Yep, there's not a
whole lot here in Lucin.

00:00:38.089 --> 00:00:40.148
Well, except for this man.

00:00:40.148 --> 00:00:42.917
(eagle screech, rattlesnake rattle)

00:00:42.917 --> 00:00:46.038
(bouncy orchestral music)

00:00:46.038 --> 00:00:48.248
But who is this man?

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:50.936
This man who lives in an airplane hangar,

00:00:50.936 --> 00:00:54.138
who flies a Cessna to get
to his closest friends,

00:00:54.138 --> 00:00:56.236
who is this man?

00:00:56.236 --> 00:00:58.229
This man who lives in
the middle of nowhere?

00:00:58.229 --> 00:01:01.635
Who lives 25 miles from this
bar with this man inside?

00:01:01.635 --> 00:01:04.081
Who owns a bunch of guns,
works with machines,

00:01:04.081 --> 00:01:05.512
and made this thing?

00:01:05.512 --> 00:01:06.845
Who is this man?

00:01:08.639 --> 00:01:12.806
- [Ivo] My name is Ivo Zdarky
and this is where I live.

00:01:13.872 --> 00:01:15.260
(quiet orchestral music)

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:16.438
- [Voiceover] As you've gathered,

00:01:16.438 --> 00:01:19.122
this man isn't from around Lucin.

00:01:19.122 --> 00:01:23.729
He grew up in Czechoslovakia
before the fall of the USSR.

00:01:23.729 --> 00:01:25.558
He didn't like it much.

00:01:25.558 --> 00:01:27.208
- [Ivo] It's kind of hard to do anything.

00:01:27.208 --> 00:01:29.881
The communists were in power there.

00:01:29.881 --> 00:01:31.711
You cannot have your own business.

00:01:31.711 --> 00:01:34.672
It's kind of difficult to fly there, so

00:01:34.672 --> 00:01:38.619
I kind of didn't feel
like I could be myself.

00:01:38.619 --> 00:01:40.381
- [Voiceover] He really
wanted to leave the country,

00:01:40.381 --> 00:01:42.062
but it wasn't easy.

00:01:42.062 --> 00:01:43.962
- [Ivo] There was Iron Curtain.

00:01:43.962 --> 00:01:46.690
They like, have machine gun towers

00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:49.029
and barbed wire to keep you in.

00:01:49.029 --> 00:01:51.339
They like to keep you.

00:01:51.339 --> 00:01:52.839
- [Voiceover] So when he was 24,

00:01:52.839 --> 00:01:55.763
he escaped the country
the only way he knew how.

00:01:55.763 --> 00:01:59.015
By flying across the border
in his self-built airplane.

00:01:59.015 --> 00:02:00.031
(ominous orchestral music)

00:02:00.031 --> 00:02:03.605
- So I drove up close to
the border between Austria

00:02:03.605 --> 00:02:06.432
and sometime like at three
o'clock in the morning

00:02:06.432 --> 00:02:09.992
I took off, and I just
glided over to Austria

00:02:09.992 --> 00:02:14.028
and I found myself Vienna
International Airport,

00:02:14.028 --> 00:02:15.732
and I landed there.

00:02:15.732 --> 00:02:19.643
And then I just showed
them my expired passport,

00:02:19.643 --> 00:02:21.560
and I asked for asylum.

00:02:22.805 --> 00:02:24.638
- [Voiceover] And the world took notice.

00:02:24.638 --> 00:02:28.009
(ominous music crescendos)

00:02:28.009 --> 00:02:31.060
- [Ivo] I guess they'd never
seen anything like that before.

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:32.859
So I think they liked it.

00:02:32.859 --> 00:02:33.692
I liked it.

00:02:33.692 --> 00:02:35.989
(laughs)

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:37.130
- [Voiceover] Ivo then moved

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:39.055
to Los Angeles, and built up a successful

00:02:39.055 --> 00:02:41.481
airplane propeller business.

00:02:41.481 --> 00:02:42.500
(thunder crashes)

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:45.852
But even LA. couldn't fit his big ideas.

00:02:45.852 --> 00:02:49.676
- [Ivo] I kind of needed a
place to test my other idea

00:02:49.676 --> 00:02:52.405
which is hard to do it in
the middle of the city,

00:02:52.405 --> 00:02:55.950
that's how I found this place in Utah.

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:59.147
It was for sale, so I bought it,

00:02:59.147 --> 00:03:02.903
and I've been here for, like, eight years.

00:03:02.903 --> 00:03:04.684
- [Voiceover] And what was Ivo's big idea

00:03:04.684 --> 00:03:06.845
that brought him to Lucin?

00:03:06.845 --> 00:03:10.076
Well, it's behind that door over there.

00:03:10.076 --> 00:03:14.243
("Trovatore, Act II,
Vedi, Le Fosche Notturne")

00:03:17.816 --> 00:03:20.704
Inside sits an eight-propeller
flying machine,

00:03:20.704 --> 00:03:23.137
able to lift off and land vertically.

00:03:23.137 --> 00:03:26.797
It's basically an
airplane-helicopter hybrid of sorts.

00:03:26.797 --> 00:03:28.186
It's kind of funny looking,

00:03:28.186 --> 00:03:31.019
but the damn thing actually flies.

00:03:35.963 --> 00:03:38.677
So what's Ivo's next big project?

00:03:38.677 --> 00:03:40.697
A solar-powered aircraft?

00:03:40.697 --> 00:03:43.054
An innovative propeller design?

00:03:43.054 --> 00:03:45.387
Some kind of new way to fly?

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:50.041
- [Ivo] The next big one
is the spear gun idea

00:03:50.041 --> 00:03:53.045
which actually, it works
better than I thought.

00:03:53.045 --> 00:03:55.161
That doesn't always work that way.

00:03:55.161 --> 00:03:57.351
Sometimes I get really bad ideas.

00:03:57.351 --> 00:03:58.218
(laughs)

00:03:58.218 --> 00:04:00.468
(drumming)

00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:02.374
- [Voiceover] Even while inventing

00:04:02.374 --> 00:04:04.557
new spear guns and the like,

00:04:04.557 --> 00:04:08.068
Ivo still finds the time
to get out of the house.

00:04:08.068 --> 00:04:09.804
In fact, that's him over there,

00:04:09.804 --> 00:04:11.757
hiking on the side of a mountain.

00:04:11.757 --> 00:04:15.436
It's just him, nature,
and his customized rifle.

00:04:15.436 --> 00:04:16.900
- [Ivo] I take the gun with me

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:18.545
because of the mountain lions.

00:04:18.545 --> 00:04:20.950
(lion growls)

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:22.827
(symbol clap)

00:04:22.827 --> 00:04:25.160
(footsteps)

00:04:27.041 --> 00:04:28.682
- [Voiceover] However
treacherous the hike,

00:04:28.682 --> 00:04:30.621
it's always worth it.

00:04:30.621 --> 00:04:33.133
You get a good view of Lucin.

00:04:33.133 --> 00:04:35.923
It actually looks pretty
nice from here, don't it?

00:04:35.923 --> 00:04:38.525
(quiet country-western music)

00:04:38.525 --> 00:04:40.985
You know, I still wonder,

00:04:40.985 --> 00:04:44.743
why did that darkling beetle
ever leave this place?

00:04:44.743 --> 00:04:47.766
Maybe Lucin wasn't right
for the little guy.

00:04:47.766 --> 00:04:49.505
Maybe it's escaping to the next place

00:04:49.505 --> 00:04:52.191
where it can be itself.

00:04:52.191 --> 00:04:56.972
For Ivo, though, looks like
this might be his last stop.

00:04:56.972 --> 00:05:00.036
- [Ivo] Kind of realized that
this is what I always wanted.

00:05:00.036 --> 00:05:02.361
I kept escaping until I escaped to Lucin,

00:05:02.361 --> 00:05:04.685
and now I don't have
anywhere else to escape.

00:05:04.685 --> 00:05:06.245
I'm kind of stuck here.

00:05:06.245 --> 00:05:08.328
(laughs)

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:11.441
- [Off Camera voice]
That was a great answer.

00:05:11.441 --> 00:05:12.707
(laughter)

00:05:12.707 --> 00:05:16.874
- Well, no, it's also a
truth, if you think about it.

